<article class="article-hero" style="padding-bottom:0;">
  <h1 style="font-size:clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.4rem); margin-top:20px;">About Mimajo</h1>
  <p class="article-meta">Asia's independently verified travel deals, published weekly.</p>
</article>

<div class="article-body">
  <p>Mimajo started with a simple frustration: travel deal sites either feel decades out of date, or they're really just ad networks wearing a "deals" costume. We wanted something in between — a site that actually checks its own deals, written by people, refreshed regularly, and built to feel like it belongs in 2026 rather than 2010.</p>

  <h2>Where the name comes from</h2>
  <p>Mimajo is three syllables, three colours: <strong>Mi</strong> (rose pink), <strong>Ma</strong> (coral peach), and <strong>Jo</strong> (deep teal). Two feminine, one masculine — a small detail, but it's baked into everything from the logo to how we think about who we're building this for: everyone who wants a good trip without overpaying for it.</p>

  <h2>How we check a deal</h2>
  <p>Every deal on Mimajo is reviewed before it's published — real prices, real availability, checked against what you'd pay booking directly. We link out to the merchant or travel partner to complete your booking; Mimajo doesn't process payments for deals itself. Some of those links are affiliate links, which is covered in full on our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure.html">Affiliate Disclosure</a> page.</p>

  <h2>Who's behind it</h2>
  <p>Mimajo is an independent, Asia-based travel publisher, currently run as a small team. We're not owned by an airline, hotel group, or booking platform — our only job is finding deals worth your time.</p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>Got a deal we should know about, a correction, or just want to say hello? Reach out via our <a href="/contact.html">contact page</a>.</p>
</div>
